{"id": "section-body-18218", "title": "Lymphomas", "chapterId": "chapter-sixteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "ORAL AND MAXILLOFACIAL CONDITIONS", "Tumours and Tumour-Like Conditions of Oral Cavity and Facial Region", "Lymphomas"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-18218", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Lymphomas", "runs": [{"text": "Lymphomas"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "1126"}}, {"id": "body-18219", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "These are group of neoplasms of varying degrees of malignancy which are derived from B-cells of lymphoid tissues, the lymphocytes and histiocytes in any of their developmental stages.", "runs": [{"text": "These"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "group"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "neoplasms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "varying"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "degrees"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "malignancy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "derived"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "from"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "B-cells"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymphoid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tissues,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the lymphocytes and histiocytes in any of their developmental stages."}]}, {"id": "body-18220", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "While lymphoma primarily affects lymph nodes, it can also occur in non-lymph node tissue (tonsils, parotid gland, thyroid gland, tongue, paranasal sinuses, and nasal cavity), this is known as extra nodal lymphoma", "runs": [{"text": "While"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymphoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "primarily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "affects"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymph"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "nodes,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "it"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "also"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occur"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "non-lymph"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "node"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tissue"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(tonsils,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "parotid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gland,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "thyroid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gland, tongue, paranasal sinuses, and nasal cavity), this is known as extra nodal lymphoma"}]}, {"id": "body-18222", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Lymphoma is classified as Hodgkin lymphoma and non-Hodgkin lymphoma.", "runs": [{"text": "Lymphoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "classified"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Hodgkin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymphoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "non-Hodgkin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymphoma."}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-18223", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Both types of Lymphoma have similar symptoms which may include but not limited to painless swelling of lymph nodes, fever, Night sweats, Unexplained weight loss, and fatigue", "runs": [{"text": "Both"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "types"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Lymphoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "have"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "similar"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptoms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "include"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "but"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "limited"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "painless"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "swelling"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymph"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "nodes,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fever, Night sweats, Unexplained weight loss, and fatigue"}]}, {"id": "body-18225", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Burkitt’s lymphoma (African Jaw Lymphoma)", "runs": [{"text": "Burkitt’s"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymphoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(African"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Jaw"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Lymphoma)"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-18226", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Burkitt lymphoma is an aggressive non-Hodgkin B-cell lymphoma characterized by rapid tumor growth, frequently affecting the jaw, abdomen, or central nervous system associated with Epstein-Barr virus (EBV).", "runs": [{"text": "Burkitt"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymphoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "aggressive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "non-Hodgkin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "B-cell"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymphoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "characterized"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rapid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tumor"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "growth,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "frequently"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "affecting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the jaw, abdomen, or central nervous system associated with Epstein-Barr virus (EBV)."}]}, {"id": "body-18227", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Three clinical subtypes: endemic, sporadic, and immunodeficiency-related. The endemic form, common in Africa, is linked to malaria and EBV,", "runs": [{"text": "Three clinical subtypes: endemic, sporadic, and immunodeficiency-related. The endemic form, common in Africa, is linked to malaria and EBV,"}]}, {"id": "body-18229", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-18230", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Confined almost exclusively to children between 2–14years of age.", "runs": [{"text": "Confined"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "almost"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "exclusively"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "children"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "between"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2–14years"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "age."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1090"}}, {"id": "body-18231", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Rapidly growing tumor mass of the jaws, destroying the bone and causing teeth loosening with extension the maxillary, ethmoid and sphenoid sinuses as well as the orbit.", "runs": [{"text": "Rapidly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "growing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tumor"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mass"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "jaws,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "destroying"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bone"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "causing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "teeth"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "loosening"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with extension the maxillary, ethmoid and sphenoid sinuses as well as the orbit."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1090"}}, {"id": "body-18232", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Visceral organ involvement may occur.", "runs": [{"text": "Visceral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "organ"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "involvement"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occur."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1090"}}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Oral and maxillofacial conditions", "start": "body-18218", "end": "body-18232"}}